UID: PLAN-V2-004
STATUS: InProgress
TITLE: M1c - Schematic capture model, ERC and interactive desktop app
STATEMENT: >>>
Build Spice.Schematic (versioned diffable document model, hierarchical subsheets, ERC, Unified Device Descriptor binding, Canonical IR emitter, SPICE/StarLark/SVG export) and the initial Spice.App desktop schematic editor and waveform cross-probing viewer backed by ISimulationBackend.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Phase: M1
Depends-on: PLAN-V2-002
Deliverables: Spice.Schematic (versioned schema 2.1 SchematicDocument with SHA-256 integrity & 2.0->2.1 migration, multi-sheet RootSheet + SubSheets with off-sheet port net bridging and private subsheet net/instance scoping, structured vector SymbolPrimitive definitions, ComponentLibraryStore with Foundation models + persistent user custom components with attached .MODEL/.SUBCKT/.OSDI models + CreateFromSchematic, SchematicCompiler with coordinate ERC, mirror/rotate transforms, grid styles, dark/light SVG themes, IEEE semiconductor/opamp/subckt & custom vector symbols, OperatingPointOverlay with active-sheet DC V/I badges, and SchematicExporter supporting SPICE3f5/ngspice/Xyce/LTspice/Spectre/StarLark-cs/multi-sheet BOM/SHA-256 Bundle exports + SPICE-to-schematic import), Spice.App runnable .NET 11 host CLI and 3-pane EDA Schematic Studio (with Multi-Sheet Tab Bar, PgUp/PgDn/Shift+H sheet navigation, and 2-Stage Cascaded RC preset) + Interactive Vector Symbol Canvas & Model Library Studio SPA consuming strictly public ``Spice.*`` APIs and libspice_capi ABI v2.1, Spice.Tests/M1PlatformTests.cs.
Verification: .NET 11.0.100 Release build (TreatWarningsAsErrors=true) passes 10/10 xUnit tests with 0 warnings on both Linux and Windows CI, verifying schema 2.1 SHA-256 save/load & tamper rejection, multi-sheet off-sheet port bridging & private net scoping with active-sheet SVG/DC V/I overlays and live C++20 simulation across sheets, fail-closed SymbolPrimitive validation and custom vector SVG rendering, multi-dialect netlist/StarLark/BOM/bundle exports, SPICE import, persistent custom component library CRUD + CreateFromSchematic, and live native C++20 simulation of custom .SUBCKT blocks (2:1 divider & Ideal Op-Amp gain=3), BSIM4 MOSFET, LTRA, and cross-probed DC V/I schematics over libspice_capi.
<<<
